# Nothing here is needed to SERVE the book — keep it out of the deployed bundle.
#
# Netlify reads .netlifyignore, Vercel reads this file, Cloudflare Pages reads
# .assetsignore; the three lists are kept identical on purpose.
#
# NOTE: these MUST sit at the REPOSITORY ROOT — that is both what a host serves and
# where it looks for this file. They used to live one level down, inside a
# "PARI'S BIRTHDAY TREASURE/" wrapper folder, and the consequence was invisible until
# production was probed: Vercel never read this file at all, so every exclusion below
# was ignored and the live site served 35.34 MB instead of 16.14 MB — the three .mp4
# masters, BGM.ogg and FLIPBOOK/tools/ were all publicly fetchable. The same offset
# left "/" with no index.html, so the site 404'd at its own root. One cause, both
# symptoms; fixed by flattening the tree. KEEP IT FLAT.
# The book reaches the game with "../MONEY%20CATCH%20MANIA/...", which climbs out of
# FLIPBOOK — so FLIPBOOK cannot be the served root either. The root is here.

# Build / conversion tooling (Node + ffmpeg, dev-machine only)
FLIPBOOK/tools/
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json

# Design docs, notes and READMEs
*.md
docs/
design/
notes/

# Backups and pre-optimisation sources. The PNG / MP4 masters the encodes were made
# from are deliberately NOT in this folder at all — they are kept outside the
# deliverable, so there is nothing here to exclude. These patterns stay as a guard
# in case one is ever dropped in beside its encode.
*.orig
*.bak
*-backup.*
assets-original/
out/
FLIPBOOK/assets/*.png
FLIPBOOK/assets/Currency/*.png

# The background-music track SHIPS AGAIN. It was excluded while BGM_VOLUME was 0 —
# that zero gated setting bgMusic.src, playBgMusic() AND the preloader entry, so no
# visitor could ever fetch it and it was 558KB of dead weight in every deploy. The
# music was turned back on (BGM_VOLUME is 0.11), so the exclusion is gone with it:
# leaving it here would have shipped a 404 instead of a soundtrack.
#
# The video masters. 1.mp4 / 3.mp4 / 4.mp4 are the H.264 sources the shipped VP9
# scenes were encoded from; nothing in the book ever requests them. They are also
# untracked now (see .gitignore), so this line is a guard rather than the mechanism.
FLIPBOOK/assets/*.mp4

# OS / editor junk
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~

# VCS + CI
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
